This bash script will present you report of your aws services usage.

Requisite:
AWSCLI - aws configuartion setup as your access user.
Ref - https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cli/latest/userguide/cli-chap-getting-started.html

Usage:
run the script in bash and it will give information as below.
- S3 Buckets - bucket list
- Instance details - Public IP and DNS name for now.
- Lambda - Functions list
- IAM - Users list

Addtionals:
You can add this script to crontab to get report frequently as reqiered.
For that crontab command and usage guidance is provides.

Output example:
-------------------------------------------------------------------
S3 Bucket Data:
--------------------------------------------------
|                   ListBuckets                  |
+------------------+-----------------------------+
|    BucketName    |          CreatedOn          |
+------------------+-----------------------------+
|  supernoa-demo-1 |  2026-02-04T07:31:44+00:00  |
+------------------+-----------------------------+
Instances Data:
-------------------------------------------------
|               DescribeInstances               |
+---------------+--------------+----------------+
|     Name      |     OS       |   PublicIP     |
+---------------+--------------+----------------+
|  devops-test-1|  Linux/UNIX  | 3x.10x.21x.x5  |
+---------------+--------------+----------------+
Functions Data:
{
    "Functions": []
}
Users Data:
{
    "Users": []
}
-------------------------------------------------------------------
